---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
const domain = site.url.replace('https://', '');
---

<Base title="Privacy" description={`Privacy policy (Datenschutzerklärung) for ${domain}.`} noindex>
  <article class="legal wrap">
    <p class="label">Datenschutzerklärung</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Short version: this website uses no cookies, no tracking across sites and no advertising. Fonts are hosted on this domain, so no requests go
      to Google or other font services.
    </p>

    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name}, contact details in the <a class="link link--under" href="/impressum">Impressum</a>. Email:
      <a class="link link--under" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      This website is delivered by Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. When you visit a page, Cloudflare processes
      technical data such as your IP address, the time of the request, the page requested and your browser’s user agent, in order to deliver the
      page securely and protect it from abuse. The legal basis is my legitimate interest in a secure, reliable website (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
      Cloudflare is certified under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework, and the transfer is also covered by EU Standard Contractual Clauses.
    </p>

    <h2>Statistics</h2>
    <p>
      I use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count page views. It sets no cookies, stores nothing on your device and does not create profiles of
      individual visitors. The legal basis is my legitimate interest in understanding how the website is used (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
    </p>

    <h2>Contact by email</h2>
    <p>
      If you email me, I use your address and message only to reply to you. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) and (f) GDPR. I delete the
      correspondence when it is no longer needed.
    </p>

    <h2>Settings stored in your browser</h2>
    <p>
      If you switch between light and dark mode, or between the canvas and list view in the playground, your choice is saved in your browser’s
      local storage. It never leaves your device and you can clear it at any time in your browser settings.
    </p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>
      Some case studies link to Figma, Google Drive or Wix. These services only receive data if you follow such a link; their own privacy
      policies apply.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You have the right to access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, data portability and objection (Art. 15–21 GDPR). You can
      also lodge a complaint with a data protection authority, for example the Bavarian Data Protection Authority (BayLDA) in Ansbach.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-top: calc(var(--header-h) + clamp(48px, 8vw, 120px));
    max-width: calc(62ch + 2 * var(--gutter));
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
    font-size: var(--t-md);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--t-2xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    line-height: 0.95;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--t-lg);
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  h2 {
    margin-top: 28px;
    font-size: var(--t-md);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
